  The difference total damage done (depending on whether there
are monsters there to take it.) between unskilled/basic and
skilled/expert for cone of cold and fireball is tremendous.  

  Not only does skilled+ cone of cold and fireball cover nine 
squares (instead of being a ray) but the amount of damage per hit
goes up.  It can go up a lot.  


  As a ray the damage per hit is
    - cone of cold: [XL/2 +1] times 6.  (NB: NOT d6)
    - fireball: 12 d6.  


  At skilled+, 
    - the damage is {[XL/2 +1] d6 } per hit.  
    - With a guaranteed nine squares being hit at least twice.  
      (It's up to you to arrange that there are monsters on 
      those squares.)
    - There may be up to a further seven occurrences of "9-square"
      (i.e. 3x3) hits.



  As a minimum, 18 hits on squares.  Maximum of 81 hits on squares.
At XL 30 with (Int > 18) that will average 50 points of damage
per hit.  Probably average five of the "9-square" occurrences per
cast.  5 x 9 x 50 gives an average of over 2000 points of damage
per cast.

  If you just get the minimum of two occurrences at XL 30 you're
still looking at over 800 points of damage.

